# CI workflows — thin-caller model: the real build+publish logic lives in the
# reusable publish.yml @main (ci.yml just calls it), so the miniapp's local copies
# don't need syncing. Also, GitHub refuses to let the sync token push changes to
# `.github/workflows/*` without the `workflows` permission — protecting them here
# avoids that wall. The gate reaches miniapps via publish.yml@main + the synced
# scripts/ (which ARE synced, since they're not workflow files).
.github/workflows/publish.yml
.github/workflows/check-compat.yml
.github/workflows/tests.yml
.github/workflows/ci.yml
.github/workflows/template-sync.yml
